### MyCrypto FastAPI v2.0 - Test Scenarios
### Complete workflow testing scenarios

### ========================================
### SCENARIO 1: Complete User & Portfolio Flow
### ========================================

### 1. Create a new user
POST http://localhost:8000/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@crypto.com",
  "name": "Alice Johnson",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123"
}

### Save the user_id from response for next requests

### 2. Verify user was created
GET http://localhost:8000/users/email/alice@crypto.com
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create crypto assets
POST http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbol": "BTC",
  "name": "Bitcoin",
  "current_price": 45000.00
}

###

POST http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbol": "ETH",
  "name": "Ethereum", 
  "current_price": 3000.00
}

### Save asset_ids from responses

### 4. Create portfolio entries for the user
POST http://localhost:8000/portfolio/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "USER_ID_HERE",
  "asset_id": "BTC_ASSET_ID_HERE",
  "quantity": 0.5,
  "purchase_price": 44000.00
}

###

POST http://localhost:8000/portfolio/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "USER_ID_HERE", 
  "asset_id": "ETH_ASSET_ID_HERE",
  "quantity": 2.0,
  "purchase_price": 2900.00
}

### 5. Get user's complete portfolio
GET http://localhost:8000/portfolio/user/USER_ID_HERE
Accept: application/json

### ========================================
### SCENARIO 2: Price Updates & Portfolio Value
### ========================================

### 1. Update Bitcoin price
PUT http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/BTC_ASSET_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_price": 47000.00
}

### 2. Update Ethereum price
PUT http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/ETH_ASSET_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_price": 3200.00
}

### 3. Check updated prices
GET http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/symbol/BTC
Accept: application/json

###

GET http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/symbol/ETH
Accept: application/json

### 4. View portfolio with updated prices
GET http://localhost:8000/portfolio/user/USER_ID_HERE
Accept: application/json

### ========================================
### SCENARIO 3: Portfolio Management
### ========================================

### 1. Add more to existing position
POST http://localhost:8000/portfolio/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "USER_ID_HERE",
  "asset_id": "BTC_ASSET_ID_HERE", 
  "quantity": 0.25,
  "purchase_price": 47000.00
}

### 2. Add new asset to portfolio
POST http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbol": "ADA",
  "name": "Cardano",
  "current_price": 0.45
}

###

POST http://localhost:8000/portfolio/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "USER_ID_HERE",
  "asset_id": "ADA_ASSET_ID_HERE",
  "quantity": 1000.0,
  "purchase_price": 0.45
}

### 3. Update portfolio entry
PUT http://localhost:8000/portfolio/PORTFOLIO_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1200.0
}

### 4. View complete updated portfolio
GET http://localhost:8000/portfolio/user/USER_ID_HERE
Accept: application/json

### ========================================
### SCENARIO 4: Error Handling Tests
### ========================================

### 1. Try to create user with duplicate email
POST http://localhost:8000/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@crypto.com",
  "name": "Another Alice",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Try to get non-existent user
GET http://localhost:8000/users/nonexistent_id
Accept: application/json

### 3. Try to create portfolio with invalid user_id
POST http://localhost:8000/portfolio/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "invalid_user_id",
  "asset_id": "BTC_ASSET_ID_HERE",
  "quantity": 1.0,
  "purchase_price": 45000.00
}

### 4. Try to get portfolio for non-existent user
GET http://localhost:8000/portfolio/user/nonexistent_user
Accept: application/json

### ========================================
### SCENARIO 5: Pagination Testing
### ========================================

### 1. Create multiple users for pagination test
POST http://localhost:8000/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@crypto.com",
  "name": "Bob Smith",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

POST http://localhost:8000/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "charlie@crypto.com", 
  "name": "Charlie Brown",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

POST http://localhost:8000/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "diana@crypto.com",
  "name": "Diana Prince", 
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Test pagination - first page
GET http://localhost:8000/users/?skip=0&limit=2
Accept: application/json

### 3. Test pagination - second page  
GET http://localhost:8000/users/?skip=2&limit=2
Accept: application/json

### 4. Test pagination with crypto assets
GET http://localhost:8000/crypto-assets/?skip=0&limit=2
Accept: application/json

